# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/careers.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event career_letter_conclave
# en: A Letter From the Seven Towers
title [843914] = 七塔来信
# en: Silver wax, seven little towers in it. The Conclave writes that Professor Thorne has mentioned your name, "more than once and without being asked", and offers you an apprenticeship at the Seven Towers after graduation. Your answer is due on the last day.
text [9fc6fa] = 银色封蜡，里面压着七座小塔。七塔议会来信说，索恩教授提过你的名字，“不止一次，而且没人问他”，并邀请你毕业后去七塔当学徒。你需在最后一天答复。
# en: A letter sealed in silver wax on a dormitory desk, seven small towers pressed into the seal.
scene [1cb250] = 宿舍书桌上一封用银蜡封口的信，封蜡上压着七座小塔。
# en: Write back that you're interested
opt.left.label [ac32a4] = 回信说你有意
# en: You write three drafts and send the shortest. Thorne passes you in the corridor the next day and says "Hm," which from him is a parade.
opt.left.say.1 [008c22] = 你写了三稿，寄出最短的那份。第二天索恩在走廊里经过你身边，说了声“嗯”，从他嘴里出来，这简直是一场游行。
# en: Ask what an apprentice actually does
opt.right.label [e09784] = 问学徒到底做些什么
# en: The answer comes by return: long hours, a grey robe, and seven years before anyone lets you near a real ward. It is less glamorous on paper. The offer stands.
opt.right.say.1 [e28410] = 回信很快：工时很长，一件灰袍，七年后才会有人让你碰真正的护界。纸面上没那么光鲜。聘约依然有效。

@event career_letter_fellowship
# en: A Fellowship at the Spire
title [c606b6] = 尖塔的研究员职位
# en: The note is inside a book you returned last week, which is how the Spire Library's fellows do things. They have a junior fellowship free, a carrel with your name already chalked on it, and a question: would you like to spend your life among books that bite? Answer by the last day.
text [f66f0c] = 字条夹在你上周还回去的一本书里，尖塔图书馆的研究员们就是这么办事的。他们空出一个初级研究员职位，一个已用粉笔写上你名字的隔间，还有一个问题：你愿意在会咬人的书中间度过一生吗？最后一天前答复。
# en: A folded note tucked inside a returned library book, written in tiny, careful faculty handwriting.
scene [bd38bb] = 一张折起的字条夹在还回去的图书馆藏书里，字迹细小而工整，是教职员的笔迹。
# en: Chalk "yes" under your name
opt.left.label [7f720d] = 在名字下写“愿意”
# en: You go down to the carrel that evening and chalk a small "yes" under your name. In the morning someone has underlined it.
opt.left.say.1 [dec700] = 那天傍晚你下到隔间，在自己名字下用粉笔写了个小小的“愿意”。第二天早上，有人在它下面画了一道线。
# en: Ask how many fellows the books have eaten
opt.right.label [d2af51] = 问书吃掉过几个研究员
# en: "Three," the reply says, "in two hundred years, and all of them were careless." You are not entirely reassured. The carrel waits.
opt.right.say.1 [92f0dd] = “三个，”回信说，“两百年里，而且都是不小心的。”你并没有完全放心。隔间在等你。

@event career_letter_shop
# en: A Lease by the Harbour
title [f6fdaf] = 港口边的租约
# en: The lease comes with a brass key and a letter from a harbour landlord whose wife swears by your hair tonic. A crooked little shop, two rooms and a still, yours from the autumn if you sign on the last day. Nobody has ever offered you a door of your own before.
text [22f9e8] = 租约附着一把铜钥匙，和一位港口房东的信，他妻子对你的生发水赞不绝口。一间歪歪扭扭的小铺子，两个房间和一口蒸馏器，只要你在最后一天签字，秋天起就归你。从来没有人给过你一扇属于自己的门。
# en: A rolled lease tied with string on a dormitory desk, a small brass key on top of it.
scene [ec5323] = 宿舍书桌上一卷用细绳扎起的租约，上面搁着一把小铜钥匙。
# en: Keep the key on a string round your neck
opt.left.label [ea40fd] = 把钥匙挂在脖子上
# en: You wear the key under your robes for the rest of the year. It's warm when you touch it, which is probably the hair tonic's doing.
opt.left.say.1 [d0ddde] = 这一年剩下的日子，你把钥匙藏在袍子底下戴着。一摸它就是温的，多半是生发水的功劳。
# en: Write back about the drains
opt.right.label [818ea0] = 回信问问下水道
# en: The landlord's reply is two pages about the drains, which you read twice. An alchemist's shop lives or dies by its drains. This one, apparently, will live.
opt.right.say.1 [61dea7] = 房东回了两页纸讲下水道，你读了两遍。一家炼金铺子的死活就看下水道。这一家，看来能活。

@event career_letter_unseen
# en: A Letter That Wasn't Posted
title [bfd784] = 一封没寄出的信
# en: The envelope is on your pillow, though the door was locked and the window shut. Inside, a single line: the Crown's Office of Unseen Affairs has a desk for you, if you want it, from the autumn. There is no address to reply to. They'll know your answer on the last day.
text [2910b8] = 信封就躺在你的枕头上，可门锁着，窗也关着。里面只有一行字：王室隐秘事务署为你留了一张书桌，如果你想要，秋天起生效。没有回信地址。最后一天，他们自会知道你的答复。
# en: A plain envelope with no stamp and no seal lying on a pillow that was empty a moment ago.
scene [8c52f6] = 一个没有邮票也没有封蜡的素信封，躺在刚刚还空着的枕头上。
# en: Leave a "yes" on the pillow
opt.left.label [bc7c45] = 在枕头上留个“好”
# en: You leave one word on the pillow and go to supper. When you come back, the paper is gone and the bed has been made. You did not make it.
opt.left.say.1 [4e7f3f] = 你在枕头上留下一个字，就去吃晚饭了。回来时，纸不见了，床也铺好了。不是你铺的。
# en: Find out how they got in
opt.right.label [6530a3] = 查出他们怎么进来的
# en: You spend a week on it and find the scratch on the window catch, the loose tile, the borrowed key. It's very good work. That's the trouble.
opt.right.say.1 [d31946] = 你花了一个星期，找到了窗闩上的划痕、松动的瓦片、借来的钥匙。手法非常漂亮。麻烦就在这儿。

@event career_letter_trading
# en: A Partnership Offered
title [aa46bb] = 一份合伙邀约
# en: A shipping house in the harbour has heard about your purse, or rather about how you filled it. Its old partner wants to retire, and offers you his desk and his share of the ledger from the autumn. "Bring your crowns," he writes. "Bring your nerve. Answer on the last day."
text [5da9ff] = 港口的一家航运商行听说了你的钱袋，准确说，是听说了你怎么把它填满的。老合伙人想退休，邀请你秋天起接下他的书桌和他在账簿里的份额。“带上你的克朗，”他写道，“带上你的胆量。最后一天答复。”
# en: A thick letter on cream paper, stamped with a shipping line's anchor, a tally of figures down its margin.
scene [ec81db] = 一封写在奶白色纸上的厚信，盖着一家航运公司的船锚印，页边写着一列数字。
# en: Write back that you're interested
opt.left.label [ac32a4] = 回信说你有意
# en: You reply on the cream paper's own back, which seems businesslike. By return comes a ledger page with a column already headed with your name.
opt.left.say.1 [9ed1bd] = 你就在那张奶白色信纸的背面回信，显得很像做生意的样子。回信寄来一页账簿，有一栏已经写上了你的名字。
# en: Ask to see the books first
opt.right.label [e8145f] = 先要看账本
# en: He sends them, all of them, and you find the hole in the third year that he hoped you'd find. "Good," says his next letter. "The last partner didn't."
opt.right.say.1 [f6ceef] = 他寄来了，全部，你在第三年那里找到了他希望你找到的窟窿。“很好，”他的下一封信说，“上一个合伙人就没找到。”

@event career_return_royal_library
# en: The Archives Write Again
title [712ad4] = 档案馆又来信了
# en: The Royal Library Archives remember your summer. The keeper writes that a cataloguer's post is free from the autumn, "for someone who reads the footnotes", and that your name was the only one proposed. Answer by the last day.
text [da3b67] = 皇家图书馆档案馆记得你的那个夏天。馆长来信说，秋天起空出一个编目员职位，“给读脚注的人”，而被提名的只有你一个。最后一天前答复。
# en: A letter in archivist's copperplate, a pressed slip of catalogue card tucked into the fold.
scene [b79102] = 一封档案员铜版体写的信，折缝里夹着一小片压平的目录卡。
# en: Write back in your best copperplate
opt.left.label [46d416] = 用最好的铜版体回信
# en: It takes an evening and four nibs. The keeper replies with a catalogue card made out in your name, under "Staff".
opt.left.say.1 [e33d71] = 你花了一个晚上和四个笔尖。馆长回了一张目录卡，上面写着你的名字，归在“职员”一栏。
# en: Ask which room you'd be given
opt.right.label [75825e] = 问会分到哪个房间
# en: "The cold one," the keeper writes, "with the folios that object to being opened." You will need gloves. You will also, you suspect, love it.
opt.right.say.1 [6d8a5f] = “冷的那间，”馆长写道，“里面的对开本都不愿被翻开。”你会需要手套。你猜，你也会爱上那里。

@event career_return_conclave
# en: The Laboratory Writes Again
title [f4b323] = 实验室又来信了
# en: The Conclave Laboratory remembers your summer, and the report your supervisor wrote at the end of it. She writes that a place as a junior researcher is yours from the autumn if you'll take it. "Don't make me ask twice," she adds. Answer by the last day.
text [ebdcbd] = 七塔议会实验室记得你的那个夏天，也记得夏末你的导师写的那份报告。她来信说，秋天起有一个初级研究员的位置，只要你肯来。“别让我问第二遍，”她补了一句。最后一天前答复。
# en: A letter on laboratory paper, slightly singed at one corner, sealed with seven small towers.
scene [22e3be] = 一封写在实验室用纸上的信，一角有点烧焦，封口压着七座小塔。
# en: Write back yes, in principle
opt.left.label [1a40b3] = 回信原则上答应
# en: You write back the same night. Her reply is one line: "Good. Bring your own gloves."
opt.left.say.1 [2093d0] = 你当晚就回了信。她的回复只有一行：“好。自带手套。”
# en: Ask what you'd be testing
opt.right.label [b27f7d] = 问要测试些什么
# en: Wards that are meant to fail, she writes, so that the ones on the city gates don't. You'd be standing very close to a great many explosions.
opt.right.say.1 [4b68d8] = 她写道，测试那些本该失败的护界，好让城门上的那些不失败。你会站得离一大堆爆炸非常近。

@event career_return_guild
# en: The Works Write Again
title [d13685] = 工坊又来信了
# en: The Guild of Alchemists' works remember your summer, and how you kept your head at the vats. The foreman writes, in a hand that has clearly been burned more than once, that a journeyman's bench is yours from the autumn. Answer by the last day.
text [7267a7] = 炼金师公会的工坊记得你的那个夏天，记得你在大缸边沉得住气。工头的字迹显然被烧过不止一回，他写道，秋天起有一张熟练工的工作台归你。最后一天前答复。
# en: A grubby letter with a chemical stain on the envelope, stamped with the Guild of Alchemists' retort.
scene [02c284] = 一封脏兮兮的信，信封上有化学药渍，盖着炼金师公会的曲颈瓶印。
# en: Write back yes, in principle
opt.left.label [1a40b3] = 回信原则上答应
# en: You write back yes. The foreman's reply is a list of protective clothing you will need to buy yourself, which you take as a welcome.
opt.left.say.1 [955eae] = 你回信说愿意。工头回了一张你得自掏腰包买的防护服清单，你把它当作欢迎词。
# en: Ask about the explosions
opt.right.label [d22aa0] = 问问爆炸的事
# en: "Two a month," he writes, "and none fatal since my father's day." You read it three times. The bench is still yours.
opt.right.say.1 [d970ed] = “一个月两回，”他写道，“从我父亲那辈起就没死过人。”你读了三遍。工作台还是你的。

@event career_return_observatory
# en: The Expedition Writes Again
title [331fc9] = 远征队又来信了
# en: The Observatory Expedition remembers your summer on the plateau. Its leader writes that next year's survey needs a chartmaker who can stay awake till dawn, and a salaried place is yours from the autumn. Answer by the last day.
text [0170e1] = 观星远征记得你在高原上的那个夏天。领队来信说，明年的测绘需要一个能熬到天亮的绘图员，秋天起有一个领薪的位置归你。最后一天前答复。
# en: A letter with a star chart sketched on the back, the paper creased from a long journey off a plateau.
scene [c98210] = 一封信，背面画着星图草稿，纸张因从高原长途寄来而起了褶。
# en: Write back yes, in principle
opt.left.label [1a40b3] = 回信原则上答应
# en: You write back under the star chart, adding one they'd missed. The leader's reply circles it twice.
opt.left.say.1 [efcb66] = 你在星图下面回信，还补上了一颗他们漏掉的星。领队的回信把它圈了两圈。
# en: Ask how cold the plateau gets
opt.right.label [558c84] = 问高原有多冷
# en: Very, is the answer, with a list of the frostbite remedies they carry. The stars, the letter adds, are worth it. You remember that they are.
opt.right.say.1 [066f1b] = 回答是：非常冷，附一张他们随身带的冻疮药清单。信上又补了一句，星星值得。你记得，确实值得。

@event career_return_field_station
# en: The Field Station Writes Again
title [0bb624] = 野外站又来信了
# en: The Beastcraft Field Station remembers your summer on the moors. The warden writes that a keeper's post is yours from the autumn, with a cottage, a lamp and more creatures than any sane person would count. Answer by the last day.
text [60182c] = 驭兽术野外站记得你在荒原上的那个夏天。站长来信说，秋天起有一个看守的职位归你，配一间小屋、一盏灯，还有正常人根本数不过来的生灵。最后一天前答复。
# en: A muddy letter with a feather pressed in it and a paw print smudged across the address.
scene [1167f9] = 一封沾着泥的信，里面夹着一根羽毛，地址上抹着一个爪印。
# en: Write back yes, in principle
opt.left.label [1a40b3] = 回信原则上答应
# en: You write back yes. The next letter has a second paw print on it, which the warden says belongs to whoever was sitting on the desk, and counts as a vote.
opt.left.say.1 [aec20d] = 你回信说愿意。下一封信上多了一个爪印，站长说那是当时坐在桌上的那位留下的，算一票。
# en: Ask about the winters
opt.right.label [e04222] = 问问冬天的情形
# en: Long, wet and lonely, the warden writes, honestly, and the best work there is. You believe the second half.
opt.right.say.1 [91d4f3] = 站长老实写道：又长又湿又孤单，也是世上最好的活儿。后半句你信。

@event career_return_thornwick
# en: Thornwick Writes Again
title [7df9d8] = 荆木又来信了
# en: Thornwick's illusion laboratory remembers your summer{flag(thornwick_offer): and the offer you kept sealed in your trunk|}. The dean writes that a researcher's bench is yours from the autumn, across the hills, among people who think glamour is a science. Answer by the last day.
text [8c4535] = 荆木学院的幻术实验室记得你的那个夏天{flag(thornwick_offer): ，还有你封在箱底的那份聘约|}。院长来信说，秋天起有一张研究员工作台归你，就在山那边，和一群认为魅影是门科学的人一起。最后一天前答复。
# en: A green-sealed letter on lacquered paper, from the rival academy over the hills.
scene [0f2d6d] = 一封写在漆光纸上的绿封蜡信，来自山那边的对手学院。
# en: Write back yes, in principle
opt.left.label [1a40b3] = 回信原则上答应
# en: You write back yes, in green ink, to annoy someone. The dean's reply says the ink was noticed and admired.
opt.left.say.1 [68c007] = 你用绿墨水回信说愿意，就为了气气某个人。院长回信说，墨水颜色有人注意到了，还很欣赏。
# en: Ask what Lumenhold would say
opt.right.label [ecf2f6] = 问流明堡会怎么说
# en: "Something cutting," the dean writes, "and then they'd hire you back at twice the salary." You suspect she's right about both.
opt.right.say.1 [68d657] = “说些尖刻话，”院长写道，“然后开双倍薪水把你请回去。”你怀疑她两样都说对了。

@event career_return_unseen
# en: The Office Writes Again
title [415c04] = 事务署又来信了
# en: A blank page, until you hold it to the candle. The Office of Unseen Affairs remembers your summer, and how few questions you asked. A desk is yours from the autumn. No reply is needed; they will know your answer on the last day.
text [11bfc4] = 一张白纸，直到你把它凑近烛火。隐秘事务署记得你的那个夏天，记得你几乎什么都没问。秋天起有一张书桌归你。无需回信；最后一天，他们自会知道你的答复。
# en: A blank sheet of paper on a desk that, held to a candle, shows writing in brown ink.
scene [88d581] = 书桌上一张白纸，凑近烛火时显出棕色墨水写的字。
# en: Burn it, as they'd want
opt.left.label [177438] = 照他们的意思烧掉
# en: You burn it over the candle and grind the ash into the grate. It feels like the first day of something.
opt.left.say.1 [f0e511] = 你在烛火上把它烧了，把灰碾进炉栅里。感觉像是某件事的第一天。
# en: Keep it, and read it again
opt.right.label [312b07] = 留着它，再读一遍
# en: You keep it, which they'll know, and read it by candle every few nights. There's a second line you missed the first time: "We'd have kept it too."
opt.right.say.1 [6e6f6e] = 你留下了它，他们会知道的，隔几晚就凑着烛光读一遍。上面还有一行你第一次漏看了：“换作我们，也会留着。”

@event career_job_spire
# en: The Stacks Want You Back
title [91692d] = 书库想留你
# en: A note under the bell on the reference desk, after your shift. The head librarian wants to keep you on after graduation, full time, as a keeper of the stacks. "Footnote has stopped biting you," it says. "That is a qualification." Answer by the last day.
text [f09636] = 下班后，咨询台的铃铛底下压着一张字条。总馆员想在你毕业后留你全职，做书库看守人。“脚注已经不咬你了，”上面写着，“这就是资格。”最后一天前答复。
# en: The library's reference desk after hours, a note left under the bell in the head librarian's careful hand.
scene [9b6321] = 闭馆后的图书馆咨询台，铃铛底下压着一张总馆员工整笔迹写的字条。
# en: Leave a note under the bell: yes
opt.left.label [47998a] = 在铃下留张字条：好
# en: You leave your answer under the bell. In the morning there's a second note: "Good. Bring a longer ladder."
opt.left.say.1 [49bb26] = 你把答复压在铃铛底下。第二天早上多了一张字条：“好。带一架更长的梯子来。”
# en: Ask about the restricted shelves
opt.right.label [740975] = 问问禁书架的事
# en: "In time," says the next note, "and only with gloves." It is not a no, and you find you're counting the years.
opt.right.say.1 [0d0b4c] = “到时候，”下一张字条说，“而且得戴手套。”这不是拒绝，你发现自己已经在数年头了。

@event career_job_newt
# en: The Landlady's Offer
title [1ffb69] = 老板娘的提议
# en: After closing, the landlady counts the till, then counts you in. She wants to keep you on after graduation, full time, behind the bar and, in a year or two, in charge of it. "You remember who ordered the spiced cider," she says. "That's rarer than magic." Answer by the last day.
text [cc0b84] = 打烊后，老板娘数完钱柜，又把你也算了进去。她想在你毕业后留你全职，站吧台，过一两年就由你来管。“你记得谁点了香料苹果酒，”她说，“这比魔法还难得。”最后一天前答复。
# en: The Gilded Newt after closing, chairs up on the tables, the landlady counting the till with a cloth over her shoulder.
scene [8da86b] = 打烊后的镀金蝾螈酒馆，椅子倒扣在桌上，老板娘肩上搭着抹布在数钱柜。
# en: Shake on it, in principle
opt.left.label [20edc8] = 原则上握手成交
# en: You shake on it over the bar. She pours you a cider on the house, which has never happened to anyone before.
opt.left.say.1 [9dd798] = 你们隔着吧台握了手。她请你喝了一杯苹果酒，这种事以前从没发生在任何人身上。
# en: Ask about the card games upstairs
opt.right.label [63786c] = 问问楼上的牌局
# en: "You'd look the other way," she says, "and so would I." The offer stands. So does the question of what you'd be looking away from.
opt.right.say.1 [6a1006] = “你会装作没看见，”她说，“我也会。”提议依然有效。你得装作没看见什么，这个问题也依然在。

@event career_job_pell
# en: The Counter at Pell's
title [53c9ea] = 佩尔家的柜台
# en: Pell's daughters ask you into the back, where Old Pell is counting drops. They want to keep you on after graduation, full time, at the counter and, one day, at the drawers that nobody else may open. "Father says you count well," says the eldest. Answer by the last day.
text [2769de] = 佩尔的女儿们把你叫到后间，老佩尔正在那里数药滴。她们想在你毕业后留你全职，守柜台，将来某一天，还要管那些别人不许打开的抽屉。“父亲说你数得好，”大女儿说。最后一天前答复。
# en: A narrow apothecary counter, a thousand labelled drawers behind it, an old man counting drops aloud at the back.
scene [ed663d] = 一条窄窄的药铺柜台，后面是上千个贴着标签的抽屉，一位老人在后头大声数着药滴。
# en: Say yes, in principle
opt.left.label [2f7cb0] = 原则上答应
# en: Old Pell stops counting long enough to nod at you, then starts again from one. His daughters say that's the highest praise there is.
opt.left.say.1 [2a018b] = 老佩尔停下来朝你点了点头，又从一开始数。他的女儿们说，这是最高的夸奖。
# en: Ask about the drawers that never open
opt.right.label [fe8db3] = 问那些从不打开的抽屉
# en: "In ten years," says the eldest, "if you're still careful." You realise you'd like to still be careful in ten years.
opt.right.say.1 [03f294] = “十年后，”大女儿说，“如果你还够仔细。”你发现，你希望十年后自己还够仔细。

@event career_job_courier
# en: A Satchel of Your Own
title [6c1996] = 你自己的挎包
# en: There's a new satchel on your peg at the loft, with your name stitched on the flap. The chief wants to keep you on after graduation, full time, flying the lake in all weathers. "The broom still pulls left," she says. "You don't." Answer by the last day.
text [a0bf81] = 阁楼里你的挂钩上挂着一个新挎包，翻盖上绣着你的名字。信使长想在你毕业后留你全职，风雨无阻地飞越湖面。“扫帚还是往左偏，”她说，“你不会。”最后一天前答复。
# en: A courier loft at dusk, brooms racked along the wall, a satchel with a newly stitched name hanging on a peg.
scene [fa81b4] = 黄昏时的信使阁楼，扫帚沿墙排开，一个新绣了名字的挎包挂在挂钩上。
# en: Sling the satchel over your shoulder
opt.left.label [41bb92] = 把挎包甩上肩
# en: It fits. You fly a lap of the lake that evening for no reason at all, and the loft cheers you down.
opt.left.say.1 [8a0e3c] = 正合适。那天傍晚你毫无理由地绕湖飞了一圈，阁楼里的人把你欢呼着迎了下来。
# en: Ask about the winter routes
opt.right.label [805575] = 问问冬天的航线
# en: The chief shows you the map of the winter routes, with the crosses where couriers came down. There are not many. There are some.
opt.right.say.1 [5e01e4] = 信使长给你看冬季航线图，上面标着信使坠落过的地方。不多。但有。

@event career_last_call
# en: The Last Call
title [58f03c] = 最后的机会
# en: Everyone else seems to have a letter. The registrar, who has seen this a hundred times, pins a short list beside her window: posts still open for this year's graduates. "Some people find their work late," she says. "Some people find it here. Some people find it in a fortnight's time, in their mother's kitchen. Choose."
text [30ff39] = 别人似乎都有了信。教务员这种事见过一百回了，她在窗边钉了一张短短的清单：今年毕业生还能去的职位。“有些人找到活儿找得晚，”她说，“有些人在这里找到。有些人两个星期后在自家妈妈的厨房里找到。选吧。”
# en: The registrar's window in the entrance hall at closing time, a short typed list of posts pinned beside it, one student left in the queue.
scene [806258] = 闭门时分入口大厅的教务窗口，旁边钉着一张打字的短清单，队伍里只剩一个学生。
# en: Go back to where you worked
opt.back.label [f226fd] = 回你干过的地方
# en: The people who know your work. A friendly interview.
opt.back.hint [1783d9] = 了解你本事的人。一场友好的面试。
# en: You knock on a door you know. The person behind it remembers you, and remembers your work better than you do. "We'd been wondering when you'd ask," they say, and write your name on a list that matters.
opt.back.say.1 [d6f6eb] = 你敲响一扇熟悉的门。门后的人记得你，记得你的活儿比你自己还清楚。“我们还在想你什么时候会来问，”对方说，然后把你的名字写在一张要紧的名单上。
# en: You knock on a door you know. They remember you warmly, and they've filled the post, last week, with someone who asked first. They wish you luck and mean it.
opt.back.say.2 [8956b8] = 你敲响一扇熟悉的门。他们热情地记得你，可职位上周已经给了一个先开口的人。他们祝你好运，是真心的。
# en: Take the registrar's list
opt.registrar.label [dd94dc] = 接下教务员的清单
# en: A clerk's post, here or in the village. Yours if you want it.
opt.registrar.hint [f820c7] = 一个书记员职位，在这里或村里。你想要就是你的。
# en: You put your name to the first post on the list: a junior clerk's desk, stamps and ledgers, a window that looks at a wall. It isn't a dream. It is a start date, and today that feels like a great deal.
opt.registrar.say.1 [35af95] = 你在清单第一项上写下名字：一张初级书记员的桌子，印章和账簿，一扇对着墙的窗。这不是梦想。但它是一个入职日期，而今天，这就很多了。
# en: Write to the post you really want
opt.reach.label [803dcc] = 写信给你真正想去的地方
# en: A long shot, in your best subject.
opt.reach.hint [fb8b24] = 孤注一掷，凭你最好的那门本事。
# en: You write the letter you'd been too proud to write at the fair, and send it before you can tear it up. A reply comes by the next owl: come and see us. You go. They say yes.
opt.reach.say.1 [4d68da] = 你写下那封在招聘会上太骄傲而没写的信，趁自己还没撕掉就寄了出去。下一只猫头鹰带来回信：来见见我们吧。你去了。他们说好。
# en: You write the letter you'd been too proud to write at the fair. The reply is kind and short, and the post went in the autumn to someone who wrote then.
opt.reach.say.2 [d70d5f] = 你写下那封在招聘会上太骄傲而没写的信。回信客气而简短，那个职位秋天就给了当时写信的人。
# en: Leave it until after graduation
opt.wait.label [d45cad] = 等毕业后再说
# en: You thank the registrar and walk away from the window. The world will still be there in a fortnight. So, she says to your back, will her list.
opt.wait.say.1 [88f56c] = 你谢过教务员，离开了窗口。两个星期后世界还在那里。她对着你的背影说，她的清单也会在。
